menu "XPRS over BLE5"

config XPRSBLE_BACKEND_TINYNIMBLE
    bool "Use tinynimble instead of the NimBLE host"
    default n
    help
        Speak to the BLE controller directly over HCI rather than through
        NimBLE. The radio behaviour is identical -- one non-connectable
        extended advertising set at 160 ms and one passive extended scan at
        0x0060/0x0050 -- and the two have been shown hearing each other on the
        air in both directions.

        Measured on a T-Deck, same board and same test, only the stack changed:
        21 KB less flash, 3.3 KB less static RAM, and 19,108 bytes less heap at
        BLE init, leaving 22,300 bytes more free at steady state.

        The catch: tinynimble has no GATT and no connections. A board that must
        serve a GATT characteristic to phones needs the NimBLE host and cannot
        use this. Everything that only broadcasts and listens can.

        Turn CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_ENABLED off as well, or the host is still linked
        and the flash saving does not appear.

endmenu
